          </p>

          <p>
            Anything thicker than a trimmer's rating is a job for another tool. Do not force it. Branches over an inch belong to loppers or a saw, and limbs overhead belong to a pole saw, which we cover in our guide to the <a href="/best-pole-saw/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold hover:underline">best pole saws</a>. Forcing thick wood into hedge trimmer teeth is the quickest way to chip a blade or strip a gearbox.
          </p>
