        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy for cut capacity first, then blade length, then the battery you already own. For most yards that means a 1-inch, 22- to 24-inch battery trimmer, and the EGO HT2411 is the one we would choose if you are starting fresh. Makita, Greenworks and BLACK+DECKER owners should stay on their platforms.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Corded is still the best value for small yards near an outlet, gas only earns its keep on long rural hedgerows, and a pole trimmer is the safe answer for anything taller than you are. Keep the blades clean and oiled, and whichever trimmer you buy will cut cleanly for years.
          </p>
